     GEBV prediction requires two essential inputs:                             
                                                                                
     1. **PLINK binary genotype files** (`--bfile`) — a .bed/.bim/.fam          
     triplet containing the genotypes of the animals you want to predict        
     breeding values for.                                                       
                                                                                
     2. **SNP effect file** (`--snp-effect`) — a tab-separated file with at     
     minimum an `id` column (SNP names matching the .bim file) and an           
     `add_a1` column (additive SNP effects).                                    
                                                                                
     You can optionally also provide:                                           
     - A list of specific sample IDs to predict (`--pred-ids`), otherwise       
     all samples in the PLINK dataset will be used.                             
                                                                                
